From: Fredrik Foss-Indrehus <fredrik@ffoss.net>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 20:28:30 +0100
Subject: Initialise the arguments in the crash handler's entry point

Started as an executable through ld.so, the library enters at
GTKNoCSDMain and its constructor never runs - glibc 2.43 does not call
the main object's constructors either, not only musl. GTKNoCSDArguments
stayed NULL, and when the application crashed the handler dereferenced
it: every restart attempt segfaulted in libgtk-nocsd.so.0 instead of
restarting the application. On Ubuntu Unity 26.04 that happened to
compiz, and to a plain GTK3 window killed with SIGSEGV.

Backported from upstream: the argument initialisation and the NULL
check. The part of the commit that strips LD_PRELOAD before starting
the handler is left out; it is for musl and needs a helper that came
with a later refactor.

Origin: backport, https://codeberg.org/MorsMortium/GTK-NoCSD/commit/d8516454a589049f6d39ced41ab45249389262b2
Applied-Upstream: 4.0
Last-Update: 2026-09-24
---
--- a/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
+++ b/Source/GTK-NoCSD.c
@@ -142,6 +142,11 @@
 void GTKNoCSDMain(void) {
 	// This runs when the library is started as an executable
 
+	// Musl does not run constructors for custom entry points
+	if (GTKNoCSDArguments == NULL) {
+		GTKNoCSDSaveArguments();
+	}
+
 	// Unset library for next start, in case of crash
 	setenv("LD_PRELOAD", "", 1);
 
@@ -164,7 +169,7 @@
 	}
 
 	// Restart if needed, leave
-	if (Restart) {
+	if (Restart && GTKNoCSDArguments != NULL && GTKNoCSDArgumentNumber > 0) {
 		printf("GTK-NoCSD: Crash detected, restarting without library.\n");
 		execve(GTKNoCSDArguments[2], GTKNoCSDArguments + 2, environ);
 	}
